<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BHP steel despatches, output down.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BHP steel despatches, output down.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd (BHP) said on Thursday its steel despatches for June slipped one percent and that its raw steel output fell five percent in June compared to June 1996.  </p>
<p>BHP pinned the decline in raw steel production mainly on lower iron ore production at its Newcastle and Whyalla works as a result of operational difficulties with blast furnaces.</p>
<p>This was only partly offset by higher steel production from from the Sydney steel mill, BHP said.</p>
<p>The production difficulties at Newcastle relate to unstable production from the Number Three blast furnace, it said.</p>
<p>&quot;It is not expected that full capacity will be achieved before early August, although this will continue to be compensated in part by higher steel production at the Sydney steel mill,&quot; BHP said.  </p>
